# Environment variables — Phase 17 Launch Readiness
# (docs/phase-17-launch-readiness/02-environment-configuration.md)
#
# Copy to `.env.local` (git-ignored) only when you have a real value.
# Never commit secrets. Never use placeholder/fake keys.
#
# Environments:
#   Development  — `.env.local` on your machine (`npm run dev`)
#   Preview      — Vercel Preview env vars (PR deployments)
#   Production   — Vercel Production env vars (main / production branch)

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Contact form (transactional email)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EMAIL_API_KEY=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vercel Analytics + Speed Insights (recommended on Vercel)
# Set to "1" in Vercel Production (and Preview if desired).
# Requires the Vercel project’s Web Analytics / Speed Insights to be enabled
# in the Vercel dashboard.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_VERCEL_ANALYTICS=1

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional second analytics vendor (GA4 or Plausible)
# Privacy-first: leave unset to skip third-party scripts.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_VENDOR=ga4 | plausible
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_ID=G-XXXXXXXX  (GA4) or yourdomain.com (Plausible)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_VENDOR=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_ID=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Error monitoring (Sentry) — optional
# Install `@sentry/nextjs` via the Sentry wizard before setting a DSN.
# Until then, errors are logged to Vercel Runtime Logs via src/lib/monitoring.ts.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Provided automatically by Vercel (do not set manually on Vercel)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VERCEL_ENV=production | preview | development
# VERCEL_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_VERCEL_ENV=
